            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "@chaul@amperecomputing.com mentioned that `$` could also be used intentionally, did you consider the case?\n\nhttps://discordapp.com/channels/775381525260664832/1402479981111676978/1406326816398115001\n\nIn that case the code should not replace it with an empty string, right?\n\nThere is patches which solve the issue by changing to `${<template_var>}` format to make the template var more explicit and also provide a boundary for start and end of the template var.\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/q/topic:%22templateVarFormat%22"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Or we could require that intentional `$` is required to be escaped?  ie. `\\$`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Or we could require that intentional $ is required to be escaped?\n\nThat's not a complete solution since we still have the issue to determine the end of the template var.\n\nSay we have `prop23` and `prop234` on DBus interface, and encounter\n\n`$prop234` somewhere, then how do we know which of those properties to substitute?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What is the solution now?  As long as the behavior is unchanged, I'm not following the concern.\n\nThis is why you shouldn't write your own parsers... but... having a \"complete parsing solution\" is kind of outside the scope of this bug fix, isn't it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I wanted to say that ChauLy already made the complete fix + migrating the configurations in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/q/topic:%22templateVarFormat%22\n\nso there is no need to make a half-solution when the complete solution is already available.\n\nAnd https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/82998 already contains a testcase as well.\n\n> This is why you shouldn't write your own parsers... but... having a \"complete parsing solution\" is kind of outside the scope of this bug fix, isn't it?\n\nThis patch simply changes the behavior without any testcase.\n\nWould have at least expected a testcase."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com, can you review my [patch](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/82998) first to see if we can reach some sort of agreement on a solution."
                },
